    "text": "Brazil’s Pix System Hit by massive Cyberattack, Transactions Suspended A major cyberattack has disrupted Brazil’s popular Pix instant payment system, leading to the suspension of transactions for customers of six financial institutions. The Central Bank of Brazil confirmed the breach and immediately severed access between the affected banks and the technology company, C&M , that suffered the initial invasion. The scale of the financial impact is still unfolding, with estimates reaching up to $800 million.\nThe attack, confirmed on Thursday, has thrown a spotlight on the vulnerabilities of Brazil’s rapidly adopted digital payment infrastructure. Pix, launched in 2020, quickly became",
